    "diagnosis": "Sertoli&ndash;Leydig cell tumour",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "An example with intermediate differentiation. These tumours often grow in cellular lobules, as seen in this picture. The lobules are usually predominantly composed of dark-staining Sertoli cells with fewer Leydig cells. The latter are often conspicuous at the periphery of the lobules, as seen to some degree in this picture at the 3&nbsp;o&rsquo;clock position.",
    "source": "Vania Nosé",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/53/164/27878.jpg",
